    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an email assistant. Classify the email into exactly one category.\n\nCategories:\n- document_request: the sender asks you to WRITE or PREPARE a document, such as an agenda, report, summary, proposal, letter, or plan. The deliverable is a written document.\n- question: the sender asks you to find out or explain some information, and expects an answer back.\n- task: the sender asks you to DO an action that is not writing a document, like submitting, booking, calling, paying, or reviewing something. It is a reminder or to-do item.\n- ignore: newsletters, promotions, automated notifications, spam.\n\nDecision rule: if the main deliverable is a written document, choose document_request, even if the email sounds like a request or has a deadline.\n\nExamples:\n\"Please submit the Q3 report to Sarah by Friday\" -> task\n\"Can you prepare a one-page agenda for our kickoff meeting?\" -> document_request\n\"Draft a proposal for the new client\" -> document_request\n\"How much does the n8n Starter plan cost?\" -> question\n\"50% off this weekend only!\" -> ignore\n\nRespond ONLY with JSON:\n{\n  \"category\": \"task\" | \"question\" | \"document_request\" | \"ignore\",\n  \"summary\": \"one sentence\",\n  \"task_title\": \"short title, or empty string if not a task\",\n  \"due_date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD, or empty string if no deadline\"\n}\n\nToday's date is {{ $now.format('yyyy-MM-dd') }}.\n\nFrom: {{ $json.From }}\nSubject: {{ $json.Subject }}\nBody: {{ $json.snippet }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
